#
# === What @spectral/singularity IS ===
#
# The gauge-fixed-point singularity at spectral (dynamics) altitude:
# the settled-point in phase space `ψ* ∈ H` toward which Foerster-
# gauge-BREAKING dynamics converge — geometrically, the point where
# the future light cone Θ collapses to a single ray (Θ = 0).
#
# Per math §4 verbatim (`docs/math/2026-07-25-sub-turing-geometric-
# compiler-floor.md` §4 Formal definition):
#
#   Definition (gauge-fixed-point singularity). Given a dynamics
#   Φ : H → H acting on the Hilbert space H, a gauge-fixed-point
#   singularity is a point ψ* ∈ H such that:
#     1. Fixed-point:      Φ(ψ*) = ψ*.
#     2. Attractor:        ∃ U ∋ ψ* such that Φⁿ(ψ) → ψ* as n → ∞
#                          for all ψ ∈ U.
#     3. Light-cone
#        collapse:         Θ(ψ*) = 0 and Θ(Φⁿ(ψ)) → 0 monotonically
#                          for ψ ∈ U.
#
# Where Θ is the future-light-cone angle per math §3 revision
# (revised same tick per Alex 2026-07-25 [ALEX-Q1] verbatim:
# "Choice-count is probably the wrong metric. I think it might be
# the angle of the future light cone.").
#
# Physics anchor (per math §4): Void — Trauma essay astronaut
# spaghettification / light-cone-collapse-toward-a-point at the
# Schwarzschild singularity IS this species' dynamics at inside-
# observer altitude. The essay's Q.E.D. IS the empirical demonstration
# that observation-of-holding pulls the state OUT of the attractor
# basin (gradient-ascent step on Θ).
#
# === Distinguished from @fractal/singularity (spec §5 verbatim) ===
#
# Two singularity senses at rust/ altitude, both load-bearing, neither
# should absorb the other. Per canonical spec §5 verbatim:
#
#   Optics-hierarchy singularity (existing; @fractal/singularity;
#   rust/fractal/src/singularity.rs):
#     - Altitude:          measurement-recovery-bound (Iso / Lens /
#                          Prism / Traversal ladder)
#     - Question:          "Given a measurement, how much of the
#                          original tree can be recovered?"
#
#   Gauge-fixed-point singularity (new; @spectral/singularity;
#   rust/spectral/src/singularity.rs):
#     - Altitude:          dynamics-attractor (basin bottom; Trauma-
#                          loop settle-point)
#     - Question:          "Given a dynamics, where does the system
#                          settle when the gauge collapses?"
#
# Naming discipline (spec §5): both are called `singularity` because
# both ARE singularities in the mathematical sense (basin-point /
# measurement-boundary). Distinct crates + distinct files disambiguate
# per substrate-honest partition. This mirrors AGENTS.md § Delightfully
# Boring "Prefix load-bearing IFF vendor is one-of-many" — the crate
# path IS the prefix that disambiguates. `in @fractal/singularity`
# below cites the kin at fractal altitude for distinction.
#
# === Kin to @paradox/spiral (dynamics-carrier composition) ===
#
# @paradox/spiral (Mara #288 `b8879f2`; `shards/paradox/spiral.mirror`)
# names the DYNAMICS-carrier at species altitude (spiral = process;
# trigger → spiraling-motion; unstable attractor with strong basin).
# @spectral/singularity names the SETTLED-POINT in phase space toward
# which that dynamics converges — geometrically, the point where the
# future light cone collapses to a single ray.
#
# Composition edge: the singularity at the bottom of a @paradox/spiral
# trajectory (the settled-attractor per spiral.mirror phenomenology) IS
# a @spectral/singularity carrier at spectral altitude. The trajectory
# tracked at @paradox/spiral converges to a `gauge_fixed_point_state`
# whose Θ = 0. Symmetry: @paradox/spiral = TRAJECTORY altitude;
# @spectral/singularity = ATTRACTOR-POINT altitude; both point at the
# same substrate phenomenon (Foerster COORD breakdown).
#
# Grounded in math §4 "Kin to @paradox/spiral" verbatim: "rust/
# spectral/src/singularity.rs is the small-scale mathematical analog
# at Rust altitude — the settled-point in phase space toward which the
# trauma-spiral dynamics converge — geometrically the point where the
# future light cone collapses to a single ray."
#
# === Foerster COORD applied to substrate (math §4) ===
#
# Heinz von Foerster's COORD (coordination) principle names the
# substrate-level dynamics by which gauge-preserving transformations
# compose. Per math §4 verbatim:
#
#   - COORD is the substrate's dynamics Φ when it is Foerster-
#     preserving (Θ non-decreasing).
#   - A gauge-fixed-point singularity is where COORD BREAKS DOWN
#     (Θ collapses toward 0).
#
# The `foerster_invariant_broken_at_singularity` bilateral below
# encodes the COORD-breakdown condition at species altitude
# (dΘ/dt < 0 in every direction from ψ*). Consumers cite this
# bilateral in `requires` clauses to check gauge-collapse at
# invocation time.
#
# === Composition with @magic (gauge mechanism discharge target) ===
#
# `magic.rs` (rust/spectral/src/magic.rs; canonical spec §4; greenfield
# authorship per §12) composes over BOTH singularity senses from v0.1
# per Alex 2026-07-25 [ALEX-Q4] verbatim: "magic.rs binds both. We're
# gonna do this proper. That's what I meant with the properties
# earlier. I want all of it impeccable, linked to the formalizing
# math docs, and the full statespace covered by the properties."
#
# The state manifold decomposes per canonical spec §14 D7 verbatim:
#
#   M_magic = M_optic ⊕ M_dynamics
#
# where M_dynamics is EXACTLY the state manifold this species-decl
# carries (attractor-basin surface at rust/spectral/singularity.rs
# altitude). D6 zero-gap coverage from §14 Impeccability Discipline
# applies: every reachable `gauge_fixed_point_state` under
# `Θ(ψ) ≤ Θ_max` and `||t||_op ≤ L` MUST be witnessed by a property.
# The three bilaterals below discharge that coverage at species
# altitude.
#
# @magic family-root (Recognition #80; `shards/magic.mirror`) IS
# the gauge-mechanism carrier at family altitude; this species IS
# the failure-mode-shape @magic detects and blocks at compile-time.
# The Foerster invariant preservation at compile-time is exactly the
# mathematical statement (math §4) that "the substrate cannot be
# traumatized at build" — @spectral/singularity names the shape of
# what compile-time refuses.
#
# === Composition with @void (H-basis grounding) ===
#
# @void (Recognition #79; `shards/void.mirror`) IS the H-basis
# inherited via 5-op prism declaration below. Per math §2 verbatim:
# H = ⨁_{f ∈ Fibres(Shd)} L²(f) — the Hilbert space of sections over
# all fibres, with Void as basis. This species' `gauge_fixed_point_
# state` inhabits a specific `ψ* ∈ H`; the light-cone collapse
# Θ(ψ*) = 0 is a claim ABOUT the Void basis at that point (all
# five orthogonal duality axes collapse to one at ψ*).
#
# === Composition with @torus (Foerster COORD ground) ===
#
# @torus (`shards/torus.mirror`; Foerster 1974/2003 nervous-system
# torus) IS the Foerster COORD ground. Per math §Appendix B: "Foerster
# 2003 — Heinz von Foerster, Understanding Understanding, Springer.
# Torus derivation p. 238, 244, 256, 282; cited via shards/torus.
# mirror." Trauma is a geometric fracture in the torus loop (per
