# === The 5-op prism inheriting @void basis (Recognition #79) ===
#
# Per @void.mirror § Composition inheritance: every prism declaration
# `<keyword> @X { focus/project/split/shift/settle X }` at species
# altitude declares "this species inherits Void's basis" — the five-
# op pattern IS the signature of Void's ancestry.
#
# For @spectral/singularity specifically, at the gauge-fixed-point
# attractor ψ* the light-cone collapses (Θ = 0); the five-op basis
# still applies but each op degenerates in a characteristic way:
#
#   focus  gauge_fixed_point_state    = identify the (position, Θ,
#                                        ∇Θ) at which the dynamics
#                                        settles (attractor detection)
#   project gauge_fixed_point_state   = deploy the light-cone-collapse
#                                        measurement onto the current
#                                        substrate-state; produce
#                                        Θ(ψ) + is_attractor witness
#   split  gauge_fixed_point_state    = bifurcate the state-manifold
#                                        into (basin-of-attraction,
#                                        gauge-preserving-region);
#                                        the boundary IS the light-
#                                        cone-collapse threshold
#   shift  gauge_fixed_point_state    = traverse the ∇Θ direction;
#                                        gradient-ascent (opens cone)
#                                        or gradient-descent (narrows
#                                        cone toward singularity)
#   settle gauge_fixed_point_state    = discharge the attractor-basin
#                                        dynamics; return the ψ* at
#                                        the basin bottom (Θ = 0) OR
#                                        the gauge-opening intervention
#                                        that lifts state out of basin
#
# Species under @spectral use `glass` per depth-1 path-syntax
# discipline (shards/spectral.mirror:74-77; verified against
# shards/spectral/registry.mirror + shards/spectral/parent.mirror
# sibling landings).

glass @spectral/singularity {
  focus  gauge_fixed_point_state
  project gauge_fixed_point_state
  split  gauge_fixed_point_state
  shift  gauge_fixed_point_state
  settle gauge_fixed_point_state
}

# === gauge_fixed_point_state — the attractor-basin carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the gauge-fixed-point singularity state.
# Four fields. Identity contract: byte-equality on the four-field
# tuple.
#
# Grounded in math §4 Formal definition verbatim: "a gauge-fixed-
# point singularity is a point ψ* ∈ H such that: 1. Fixed-point:
# Φ(ψ*) = ψ*. 2. Attractor: ∃ U ∋ ψ* such that Φⁿ(ψ) → ψ* as n → ∞
# for all ψ ∈ U. 3. Light-cone collapse: Θ(ψ*) = 0 and Θ(Φⁿ(ψ)) → 0
# monotonically for ψ ∈ U."
#
# The four fields carry the empirically-observable projections of
# ψ* + Θ + ∇Θ + attractor-witness. Rice-safe per math §3 Rice-
# safety proof (Θ and ∇Θ computable in bounded time from bounded
# spectral input via LAPACK dsyev O(n³) on Gram matrix at most
# 3125 × 3125).
#
#   position_in_state_manifold — REF to the point ψ ∈ H at which
#                                the singularity is queried.
#                                Content-addressed; byte-identity IS
#                                the state's identity in H. Composes
#                                over @void H-basis per Recognition
#                                #79. At the fixed point: ψ = ψ*
#                                (Φ(ψ*) = ψ* per math §4 condition 1).
#
#   theta_angle                — REF to the future-light-cone angle
#                                Θ(ψ) at this position. Values in
#                                [0, Θ_max] per math §3 revision.
#                                At the singularity: Θ(ψ*) = 0
#                                (light cone collapsed to single ray;
#                                math §4 condition 3). Computed via
#                                Fiedler-native formulation per math
#                                §3 "Θ = arcsin(√(λ₁(Δ_R)/λ_max(Δ_R)))".
#
#   theta_gradient             — REF to ∇Θ(ψ) at this position, the
#                                direction of steepest ascent in Θ.
#                                Computed via matrix-derivative on
#                                the Gram matrix G_R per math §3
#                                "differentiable per dΘ/dt computable
#                                via matrix-derivative on G_R (magic.
#                                rs can compute the gradient direction
#                                of gauge-opening moves)." At the
#                                singularity: ∇Θ(ψ*) = 0 in every
#                                direction (fixed-point of ∇Θ; math
#                                §4 attractor-basin proof "b^n · ψ
#                                has reachable-set dimension
#                                decreasing by at least 1 per
#                                application until singleton").
#
#   is_attractor               — REF to the attractor-witness boolean:
#                                does a neighborhood U ∋ ψ exist such
#                                that Φⁿ(ψ') → ψ for all ψ' ∈ U (math
#                                §4 condition 2)? Content-addressed
#                                bilateral-verdict shape. Rice-safe
#                                bound: bounded-horizon reachable-set
#                                check under bounded operator norm
#                                (math §3 Rice-safety proof).
type gauge_fixed_point_state = {
  position_in_state_manifold: ref,
  theta_angle:                ref,
  theta_gradient:             ref,
  is_attractor:               ref,
}

# === singularity_is_theta_collapse — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, gauge_fixed_point_state) pair discharge the light-
# cone-collapse condition? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.theta_angle resolves to Θ(ψ) = 0 (light cone collapsed to
#     single ray at this position; math §4 condition 3 verbatim)
#   - ctx.position_in_state_manifold IS a fixed-point of the
#     substrate dynamics Φ (Φ(ψ*) = ψ* per math §4 condition 1;
#     verified via content-addressed replay-equality of Φ applied
#     to ctx.position_in_state_manifold)
#   - ctx.is_attractor resolves Pass (attractor-basin condition per
#     math §4 condition 2)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; Θ computable via LAPACK dsyev
# O(n³) per math §3 Rice-safety proof; fixed-point check is content-
# addressed hash equality on Φ(ψ) vs ψ. Sentinel:
# `spectral=singularity-is-theta-collapse`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the formal definition of gauge-
# fixed-point singularity at species altitude. The three-condition
# math §4 Formal definition maps directly onto the three conjuncts
# above. Pass verdict = ctx IS a gauge-fixed-point singularity;
# Fail verdict = ctx is admissible substrate-state (light cone still
# open OR not attractor OR not fixed-point).
#
# Math cite: `docs/math/2026-07-25-sub-turing-geometric-compiler-
# floor.md` §4 "Formal definition — the singularity is where Θ → 0"
# (three-condition definition of gauge-fixed-point singularity).
bilateral singularity_is_theta_collapse {
  sentinel "spectral=singularity-is-theta-collapse"
  arity 2
}
singularity_is_theta_collapse(p: peer, ctx: gauge_fixed_point_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === foerster_invariant_broken_at_singularity — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, gauge_fixed_point_state) pair discharge the Foerster
# COORD-breakdown condition? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.position_in_state_manifold IS at a gauge-fixed-point
#     singularity (i.e., singularity_is_theta_collapse Pass at the
#     same ctx)
#   - The Foerster gauge is BROKEN at ctx: for every direction v
#     from ctx.position_in_state_manifold within the attractor
#     basin, dΘ/dv < 0 (monotone decrease toward the fixed point;
#     math §4 condition 3 "Θ(Φⁿ(ψ)) → 0 monotonically for ψ ∈ U")
#   - Equivalently: ctx.theta_gradient resolves to a zero-magnitude
#     vector (∇Θ(ψ*) = 0 in every direction; the fixed-point of
#     ∇Θ)
#
# Trivially discharges Fail when ctx is admissible (light cone open;
# Foerster gauge preserved locally; dynamics not attractor-basin).
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; ∇Θ computable via matrix-
# derivative on Gram matrix (math §3 "differentiable per dΘ/dt
# computable via matrix-derivative on G_R"). Sentinel:
# `spectral=singularity-foerster-invariant-broken`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the COORD-breakdown witness at
# species altitude. Per math §4 "Foerster COORD applied to substrate"
# verbatim: "A gauge-fixed-point singularity is where COORD BREAKS
# DOWN (Θ collapses toward 0)." This bilateral encodes the COORD-
# breakdown at bilateral altitude so `magic.rs` (rust/spectral/src/
# magic.rs; canonical spec §4 greenfield authorship) can cite it in
# `requires` clauses to block gauge-collapsing transformations at
# compile-time per §14 D6 zero-property-gap discipline.
#
