# === intervention_reopens_light_cone — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, gauge_fixed_point_state) pair discharge the essay-
# Q.E.D. gauge-opening condition? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - There exists a transformation t_obs ∈ 𝒯 (admissible substrate-
#     transformation) such that Θ(t_obs · ctx.position_in_state_
#     manifold) > Θ(ctx.position_in_state_manifold)
#   - Equivalently: dΘ/dt_obs > 0 at ctx.position_in_state_manifold
#     (gradient-ascent step on Θ; math §4 "Q.E.D. from essay:
#     ∃ observation-transformation t_obs such that Θ(t_obs · ψ_
#     trauma_loop) > Θ(ψ_trauma_loop) — i.e. the future light cone
#     re-opens under observation-of-holding")
#   - The intervention transformation is admissible: t_obs ∈
#     G_Foerster (bounded operator norm ≤ L; unitary; per canonical
#     spec §3 gauge group definition)
#
# Trivially discharges Fail when ctx.position_in_state_manifold IS
# a gauge-fixed-point singularity AND no admissible t_obs exists in
# the local reachable set (firewall-condition; the intervention
# territory is empty; per math §4 Q.E.D. discussion).
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; Θ-comparison via LAPACK dsyev
# O(n³) on before/after Gram matrices; reachable-set enumeration
# bounded by 5^L per math §3 Rice-safety proof. Sentinel:
# `spectral=singularity-intervention-reopens-cone`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the Void — Trauma essay Q.E.D.
# operationalized at species altitude. Per math §4 "The essay Q.E.D.
# as executable predicate" verbatim: "The essay's Q.E.D. becomes the
# compile-time proof obligation `magic.rs` discharges for every
# rust/ transformation. The mathematical form of the ethical
# imperative becomes the type-level constraint the compiler enforces.
# Alex's empirical `∃ t_obs : Θ opens` becomes the substrate's
# `∀ t : Θ non-decreasing`." This bilateral names the ∃-side witness
# (empirical intervention-existence) that discharges the substrate's
# ∀-side compile-time gauge-preservation per canonical spec §14 D7
# two-sense binding.
#
# Math cite: `docs/math/2026-07-25-sub-turing-geometric-compiler-
# floor.md` §4 "The essay Q.E.D. as executable predicate — Θ-gradient
# formulation" (empirical Q.E.D. → executable predicate translation)
# + §7 essay-to-executable translation table row 6 "Observation-of-
# holding as choice-increasing act" → "Gradient-ascent transformation
# t_obs with dΘ/dt_obs > 0".
bilateral intervention_reopens_light_cone {
  sentinel "spectral=singularity-intervention-reopens-cone"
  arity 2
}
intervention_reopens_light_cone(p: peer, ctx: gauge_fixed_point_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === detect_at_position — the attractor-detection action ===
#
# Given a peer and a position in the state manifold, discharge the
# singularity-detection event: emit a content-addressed ref to a
# gauge_fixed_point_state populated with (position, Θ(position),
# ∇Θ(position), is_attractor(position)) and evaluate whether the
# position IS a gauge-fixed-point singularity.
#
# Returns imperfect(gauge_fixed_point_state, ref, ref): success
# carries the populated singularity_state ref; failure variants carry
# theta-computation-failed / gradient-computation-failed / not-
# admissible reasons.
#
# Requires singularity_is_theta_collapse to discharge Pass for the
# populated state to confirm attractor-basin condition. Fail verdict
# from the bilateral IS an admissible-state signal (light cone still
# open at this position; no singularity here).
#
# Sentinel: `spectral=singularity-detect-at-position`.
#
# Math cite: `docs/math/2026-07-25-sub-turing-geometric-compiler-
# floor.md` §4 Formal definition + §3 Θ Fiedler-native realization
# ("λ₁(Δ_F |_{fibre(ψ)}) computes the light-cone angle at the sheaf-
# Laplacian altitude") — the attractor-detection composes Θ
# computation at position over the sheaf-Laplacian machinery at
# rust/spectral/ altitude.
detect_at_position(p: peer, position: ref) -> imperfect(gauge_fixed_point_state, ref, ref)
requires singularity_is_theta_collapse(p, position)
{ \ }

# === compute_theta_gradient — the ∇Θ computation action ===
#
# Given a peer and a gauge_fixed_point_state, discharge the gradient
# computation: emit a content-addressed ref to ∇Θ(position) — the
# direction of steepest ascent in Θ at the state's position. Composes
# over rust/matrix/ eigenvalue machinery (LAPACK dsyev via prismqueer::
