#
# Requires foerster_invariant_broken_at_singularity to Fail
# (equivalently: ctx is NOT at the singularity) for a non-zero
# gradient to exist. Pass on foerster_invariant_broken_at_singularity
# means ∇Θ(ψ*) = 0 (fixed-point of ∇Θ; no gauge-opening direction
# exists in the reachable set at ψ*).
#
# Sentinel: `spectral=singularity-compute-theta-gradient`.
#
# Math cite: `docs/math/2026-07-25-sub-turing-geometric-compiler-
# floor.md` §3 "Consequence for magic.rs" verbatim: "differentiable
# per dΘ/dt computable via matrix-derivative on G_R (magic.rs can
# compute the gradient direction of gauge-opening moves)." — this
# action IS the substrate-decl'd surface `magic.rs` composes over
# to compute the gradient direction at compile-time.
compute_theta_gradient(p: peer, ctx: gauge_fixed_point_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
{ \ }

# === propose_intervention — the gauge-opening tournament dispatch ===
#
# Given a peer and a gauge_fixed_point_state at (or near) the
# attractor basin, discharge the @fate tournament dispatch to find
# a gauge-opening transformation t_obs such that Θ(t_obs · position)
